{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "section_title", "parent_tag": "01R5", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\section{", "suffix": "}\n\\label{section-scheme-theoretic-image}"}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:87641287766ef916642ac0c796c57f77b58cb818ebfee6055fe570f35c62b21c", "source_text": "Scheme theoretic image", "source_text_hash": "sha256:4387c3a0a16d1f15eddb1010c1ceadb502ab5ab284a2e79583fad0a73f625295", "unit_id": "tag:01R5:title"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "01R5", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:bd0672bc61e1109de675396e5e2b978b6e92d9e552431161166c9c0fb8584c7a", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nCaution: Some of the material in this section is ultra-general and\nbehaves differently from what you might expect.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:00be1ad0c0904f8c17e0ec002c528c0be6b0c52f43d6323f0348338e3ce76b07", "unit_id": "tag:01R5:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "01R5", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : X \\to Y$", "MATH_0002": "$Z \\subset Y$", "MATH_0003": "$f$", "MATH_0004": "$Z$", "MATH_0005": "$Z' \\subset Y$", "MATH_0006": "$f$", "MATH_0007": "$Z'$", "MATH_0008": "$Z \\subset Z'$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-scheme-theoretic-image}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:74b0af77fe89c61e79e46738581d232c10e9d515160261c2b06ca949f4f01a74", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:02b30197272cb3a189db7a1fbb5f38fec5083064993e784e361d3a6f0dda068b", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a morphism of schemes. There exists a closed\nsubscheme <MATH_0002> such that <MATH_0003> factors through <MATH_0004> and such\nthat for any other closed subscheme <MATH_0005> such that <MATH_0006>\nfactors through <MATH_0007> we have <MATH_0008>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:2c05fb26d4f4b9ba65a67bf95d203bce451ed5da4126dd6c378d991fb18fba2e", "unit_id": "tag:01R6:statement"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "01R5", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{I} = \\Ker(\\mathcal{O}_Y \\to f_*\\mathcal{O}_X)$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{I}$", "MATH_0003": "$Z$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{I}$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{I}'$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{I}$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-closed-immersion-bijection-ideals}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-closed-immersion-ideals}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{lemma-largest-quasi-coherent-subsheaf}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:a25c727de132b378641e625397b6e5620aac9cb79dac347ee5731f1961512e14", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:ff4b903a0db0f14182f71b60c9c4505bda81ec1b3bf7e691327cb6e41f164015", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001>.\nIf <MATH_0002> is quasi-coherent then we just take <MATH_0003> to be the\nclosed subscheme determined by <MATH_0004>, see\nLemma <REF_0001>. This works by\nLemma <REF_0002>.\nIn general the same lemma requires us to show that there exists\na largest quasi-coherent sheaf of ideals <MATH_0005> contained in\n<MATH_0006>.\nThis follows from Lemma <REF_0003>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:d6c747c45e75f41f352afae09beb86f0a5b18c380d0f7f7d2126916ef7f5c950", "unit_id": "tag:01R6:proof"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "01R5", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : X \\to Y$", "MATH_0002": "$f$", "MATH_0003": "$Z \\subset Y$", "MATH_0004": "$f$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-scheme-theoretic-image}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-scheme-theoretic-image}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:465ed6d9e6ce29e30d5fce04c3f8c4fa55931bd4a80a10d93be3461c7e2a2b59", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:5ac49da6b9f752a75db5de2cd039dbea97f600d41eb972ef4e51987fc8b67bf8", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a morphism of schemes. The <TEXTITOPEN_0001>scheme theoretic image<TEXTITCLOSE_0001>\nof <MATH_0002> is the smallest closed subscheme <MATH_0003> through which <MATH_0004>\nfactors, see Lemma <REF_0001> above.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:03fe6329eefef7210ee8d5ef6ce3768f44d4b61f8404925f70a6bfba75155f8f", "unit_id": "tag:01R7:statement"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "01R5", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : X \\to Y$", "MATH_0002": "$Z$", "MATH_0003": "$f : X \\to Z$", "MATH_0004": "$f$", "MATH_0005": "$f$", "MATH_0006": "$\\overline{f(X)} \\subset Z$", "MATH_0007": "$f(X) \\subset Z$", "MATH_0008": "$Y$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{examples-section-scheme-theoretic-image}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{examples-section-strange-immersion}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent", "STRUCT_0002": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\item", "STRUCT_0005": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:37cf1468051e19930aec1671e47102f796e675b7ac8ebe13fb4719388186d0f6", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:4e207a49356854d7e58656daa4decb4ee6610b47039d9bd1bc5f110f7d5f3bb4", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nFor a morphism <MATH_0001> of schemes with scheme theoretic image <MATH_0002>\nwe often denote <MATH_0003> the factorization of <MATH_0004>\nthrough its scheme theoretic image. If the morphism <MATH_0005> is not\nquasi-compact, then (in general)\n<STRUCT_0002>\n<STRUCT_0003> the set theoretic inclusion <MATH_0006>\nis not an equality, i.e., <MATH_0007> is not a dense subset, and\n<STRUCT_0004> the construction of the scheme theoretic image does not commute with\nrestriction to open subschemes to <MATH_0008>.\n<STRUCT_0005>\nIn Examples, Section <REF_0001>\nthe reader finds an example for both phenomena.\nThese phenomena can arise even for immersions, see\nExamples, Section <REF_0002>.\nHowever, the next lemma shows that both disasters are avoided\nwhen the morphism is quasi-compact.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:d9ea37737329a8de5a312789554df0332fdee19b667002423bd5f0209f091b9b", "unit_id": "tag:01R5:prose-0002"}
